	"note": "Design map (M18.1, ADR 0028). The hall at the bottom of the hidden chute (4.37 O): piles of scraped bones, a skull on each, swept and kept up; centuries old and mostly Raskghar, no Minotaur bones. Pisces thinks it was a disposal chute later used as a burial room. The pile under the chute is smashed and a path of knocked-over piles leads to the one exit, where a Raskghar skeleton lies with a broken-haft battleaxe in its chest. Beyond it a long corridor of uneven tiles with a trap leads down into the dungeon (here: liscor_crypt). Guesses: the layout, the number of piles, the corridor's shape and the trap.",
